        {
          "entry_id": 2840,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.5916686,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do I need a referral from a primary care doctor to book with a specialist?\nAnswer: You can book a visit with any of our practitioners without a referral.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2857,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.36382908,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Medical examinations for work, driving and sport\n\nWe do not carry out commercial driver (DOT) medical examinations, pilot medicals or immigration medical examinations. A sports physical before joining a team or a competition is done in a standard GP appointment.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2844,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.35992444,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insurer for potential reimbursement.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2845,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3298838,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other specialist consultations.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2858,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.31263316,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2857,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.31254423,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Long-term conditions\n\nIf you live with a long-term condition such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, asthma or COPD, your GP will agree a regular review schedule w",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2841,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.31086317,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I bring to my first appointment?\nAnswer: Please bring a valid photo ID, your insurance card, and any relevant prior lab or test results related to your case.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2842,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.30461168,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do you offer virtual or telehealth consultations?\nAnswer: No, we currently only offer in-person visits at our clinic location.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2856,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.30207002,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## Conversations with the chat assistant\n\nConversations with the clinic's chat assistant are kept with your appointment records. Clinic staff can read them, ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2851,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3014222,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n\nSome tests are done at the clinic during a regular appointment. This guide explains how to prepare for each of them. If your doctor has given you different instruc",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2854,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.29671437,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Messages we will never send\n\nWe will never ask for your card number, bank details, Social Security number or insurance member ID by text message",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2856,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.29616892,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## Who can see your medical record\n\nYour record can be seen only by the practitioners and staff involved in your care at the clinic, and by the staff who han",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.29153186,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Medicare and Medicaid\n\nWe accept Original Medicare (Part B) for medical visits. Medicare does not cover routine dental care, so dental appointments are self-pay for Medicare ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2855,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.28707847,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Registering as a new patient\n\nNew patients fill in three forms at their first visit:\n\n- Form PR-1, New Patient Registration: your contact details, emergency contact an",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2854,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.28410292,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Phone calls\n\nIf we cannot reach you by phone, we leave a voicemail with only the clinic's name, a callback number and your first name - never th",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2856,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.28358573,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## Questions and complaints about privacy\n\nOur privacy officer answers questions about how your information is used and handles privacy complaints. Ask the f",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2854,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.28303853,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Email\n\nWe use email only to confirm a new appointment and to send an itemized receipt you have asked for. We do not send test results or medical",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2856,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.28253502,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## Recording a consultation\n\nYou may make an audio recording of your own consultation for your personal use, as long as you tell the practitioner before you ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2850,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.2774994,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## Feeling anxious about the dentist\n\nLet us know when you book or when you check in. The dentist will agree a stop signal with you - raising your left hand - and will pause whenev",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2855,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.27501756,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Language interpreters\n\nFree telephone interpreting is available in more than 200 languages for any appointment. Ask for it when you book or when you check in; there is",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2850,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": 0.2738272,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## Services we do not offer\n\nWe do not offer teeth whitening, orthodontic treatment such as braces or clear aligners, or dental implants.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2853,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27214926,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Running late\n## If you are running late\n\nCall the front desk on (212) 555-0142 as soon as you know you will be late, so we can tell the practitioner and plan around it. The phone line is answered Mo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2855,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.26573095,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Bringing someone with you\n\nYou may bring one adult companion into the consulting room. Anyone else who comes with you can wait in the waiting area.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2857,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.25806016,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Annual physical examination\n\nAn annual physical is a preventive check-up for adults who feel well. It includes a review of your medical history and current medicines; yo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2849,
